- ### An expiring value
+ ### Un valor que caduca

- A `Cache` remembers one value, with a lifetime after which it is computed again. The
- lifetime is any [duration](time.md#durations-and-timespans), here a
- [quantity](quantities.md) of seconds, with the import which lets a `Cache` read it. The type
- of the cached value is stated in the expected type:
+ Una `Cache` recuerda un valor, con una vida útil tras la cual se vuelve a calcular. La vida útil
+ es cualquier [duración](time.md#durations-and-timespans), aquí una [magnitud](quantities.md) en
+ segundos, con la importación que permite a una `Cache` leerla. El tipo del valor en caché se
+ indica en el tipo esperado:

= of the cached value is stated in the expected type:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- import durationInterfaces.aviationDuration
+ import durationInterfaces.aviationDuration

- case class Configuration(port: Int)
+ case class Configuration(port: Int)

- var loads = 0
+ var loads = 0

- def loadConfiguration(): Configuration =
+ def loadConfiguration(): Configuration =

-   loads += 1
+   loads += 1

-   Configuration(8080)
+   Configuration(8080)

- val config: Cache[Configuration] = Cache(300.0*Second)
+ val config: Cache[Configuration] = Cache(300.0*Second)

= val config: Cache[Configuration] = Cache(300.0*Second)
- ```
+ ```

- `establish` gives the current value. It computes the value only when none is held, or when
- the one which is held has expired. Here the second call gives the same value, and will until
- five minutes pass:
+ `establish` da el valor actual. Solo calcula el valor cuando no hay ninguno, o cuando el que hay
+ ha caducado. Aquí la segunda llamada da el mismo valor, y lo seguirá dando hasta que pasen cinco
+ minutos:

= five minutes pass:
=
