+ ```scala fuel

= five minutes pass:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= five minutes pass:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

= ##
- Out.println(config.establish(loadConfiguration()).inspect)
+ Out.println(config.establish(loadConfiguration()).inspect)

= Out.println(config.establish(loadConfiguration()).inspect)
- Out.println(config.establish(loadConfiguration()).inspect)
+ Out.println(config.establish(loadConfiguration()).inspect)

- Out.println(loads.show)
+ Out.println(loads.show)

= Out.println(loads.show)
- ```
+ ```

- The computation runs under a lock. When the value is missing or expired, and several threads
- ask at once, one computes, and the rest receive its result. That prevents the
- [stampede](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cache_stampede) which a bare lazy value cannot.
- [Concurrency](concurrency.md) describes the tasks which might be asking.
+ El cálculo se ejecuta bajo un bloqueo. Cuando el valor falta o ha caducado, y varios hilos lo
+ piden a la vez, uno lo calcula y los demás reciben su resultado. Eso evita la
+ [estampida](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cache_stampede) que un simple valor perezoso no puede
+ evitar. [Concurrencia](concurrency.md) describe las tareas que podrían estar pidiéndolo.

- A `Cache` which is created without a lifetime, as `Cache[Configuration]()`, computes its
- value once, and keeps it.
+ Una `Cache` creada sin vida útil, como `Cache[Configuration]()`, calcula su valor una vez y lo
+ conserva.

- ### Related
+ ### Relacionado

- - [Bloom filters](bloom-filters.md) remember only whether something has been seen.
- - [Filesystem](filesystem.md#content-addressed-storage) describes a cache on disk, keyed by
-   the digest of its content.
- - [Time](time.md) describes the durations which a lifetime is given in.
- - [Stack traces](stack-traces.md) describes the codepoint which keys a cached value to its call site.
+ - [Filtros de Bloom](bloom-filters.md) solo recuerdan si algo se ha visto.
+ - [Sistema de ficheros](filesystem.md#content-addressed-storage) describe una caché en disco,
+   indexada por el resumen de su contenido.
+ - [Tiempo](time.md) describe las duraciones en las que se da una vida útil.
+ - [Trazas de pila](stack-traces.md) describe el punto de código que asocia un valor en caché a
+   su punto de llamada.
